  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable infrastructure and road construction technology roadcem</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Note: This project has been cancelled, because the partners were not able to continue to work in South Sudan.Road infrastructure is crucial for private sector development. The road density in South Sudan is the lowest in Sub-Sahara Africa and among low-income states. Infrastructure is an investment priority for the coming years. Present road construction techniques in Sudan are costly because all raw materials have to be imported and works can only be executed in the dry season. The project introduces a new sustainable technology for durable and flood-proof road construction and terrain pavement. This proven technology allows for quick all-year round, on the spot blending with local, onsite materials for road and terrain stabilisation without the need to road bed excavation.The project will be located in Juba.The applicant is Jonk B.V., a Dutch company active in construction of infrastructure (roads and sewerage) small-scale dredging, soil redemption and rental of excavation machinery.The first local partner is East African Machinery Ltd (EAM) and is active in road contracting, equipment rental and personnel training.The second local partner is Marine Middle East Trading FZE with main activities: trading, service, training and management in the field of infrastructure and dredging.The partners will establish and register a joint venture in South Sudan in the form of a limited company called CONS-STRUCT.The joint venture will focus their activities in the first years on subcontracting and on road construction in Juba and direct surroundings.</narrative>
  </description>
